Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 07:21:49 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 26/34] Assemble NSS ppc-gcm.S with clang's integrated
 assembler

The file names the stack and TOC pointers with ".set SP, 1" and
".set TOCP, 2". GNU as accepts those symbols as register numbers in
memory operands; clang's integrated assembler rejects "-8(SP)" as an
invalid memory operand, which is why clang builds have needed the
system NSS so far. Define the two names with the preprocessor instead,
so both assemblers see numerals. GNU as produces identical code.
---
 security/nss/lib/freebl/ppc-gcm.S | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/security/nss/lib/freebl/ppc-gcm.S b/security/nss/lib/freebl/ppc-gcm.S
index 8447821..523eb7e 100644
--- a/security/nss/lib/freebl/ppc-gcm.S
+++ b/security/nss/lib/freebl/ppc-gcm.S
@@ -4,8 +4,8 @@
 
 # Registers:
 
-.set SP, 1
-.set TOCP, 2
+#define SP 1
+#define TOCP 2
 
 .macro VEC_LOAD_DATA   VR, DATA, GPR
     addis        \GPR, 2, \DATA@got@ha
